1
00:15:21,818 --> 00:15:27,818
Los Angeles Plays Itself is a documentary film directed by Thom Andersen.

2
00:30:43,636 --> 00:30:49,636
From its distinctive neighborhoods to its architectural homes, Los
Angeles has been the backdrop to countless movies.

3
00:46:05,454 --> 00:46:11,454
In this dazzling work, Andersen takes viewers on a whirlwind tour through the metropolis' real and cinematic history, investigating the
myriad stories and legends that have come to define it, and meticulously, judiciously revealing the real city that lives beneath.

4
01:01:27,272 --> 01:01:33,272
Narrator (voice), played by Encke King.

5
01:16:49,090 --> 01:16:55,090
Officer Frank Smith in Dragnet (archive footage), played by Ben Alexander.

6
01:32:10,909 --> 01:32:16,909
Frank Stark in Rebel Without A Cause (archive footage), played by Jim Backus.

7
01:47:32,727 --> 01:47:38,727
Lana Turner in L.A. Confidential (archive footage), played by Brenda Bakke.

8
02:02:54,545 --> 02:03:00,545
Dorothy in Bush Mama (archive footage), played by Barbara O. Jones.

9
02:18:16,363 --> 02:18:22,363
Dr. Clayton Forrester in The War of The Worlds
(archive footage), played by Gene Barry.

10
02:33:38,181 --> 02:33:44,181
Los Angeles Plays Itself is an American essay film by Thom Andersen, finished in
2003, exploring the way Los Angeles has been presented in movies.
